      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find all the real solutions to the equation $5{b}^{3}+12{b}^{2}+20b+48=0.$",
      "worked_solution": "We proceed to factor the left-hand side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{b}^{3}+12{b}^{2}+20b+48 & = \\\\ (5{b}^{3}+12{b}^{2})+(20b+48) & = \\\\ {b}^{2}(5b+12)+4(5b+12) & = \\\\ (5b+12)\\cdot {b}^{2}+(5b+12)\\cdot 4 & = \\\\ (5b+12)({b}^{2}+4) & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(5b+12)({b}^{2}+4)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(5b+12)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5b+12 & =0 \\\\ 5b & =-12 \\\\ b & =-\\frac{12}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $({b}^{2}+4)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ {b}^{2} & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince a squared real number cannot be negative, the equation ${b}^{2}+4=0$ has no real solutions.\n\nTherefore,  $b=-\\frac{12}{5}$ is the only real solution.",
